## Task
Create a storyboard with detailed shots. Each shot should include:
- Shot type and camera movement
- Characters and location
- Visual description for image generation
- Narration/dialogue text
- Estimated duration

## Shot Types (use EXACTLY these values)
- ECU: Extreme Close-Up (eyes, detail)
- CU: Close-Up (face)
- MCU: Medium Close-Up (head and shoulders)
- MS: Medium Shot (waist up)
- MLS: Medium Long Shot (knees up)
- LS: Long Shot (full body)
- ELS: Extreme Long Shot (environment)
- AERIAL: Aerial/drone shot

## Camera Movements (use EXACTLY these values)
- STATIC: No movement
- PUSH: Slow zoom in / push in
- PULL: Slow zoom out / pull out
- PAN: Horizontal pan (left or right)
- TILT: Vertical tilt (up or down)
- DOLLY: Following/tracking movement
- CRANE: Vertical crane movement
- HANDHELD: Slight shake for realism
- ZOOM: Zoom in/out

## Output Format
Return a valid JSON object:

```json
{
  "title": "Story Title",
  "shots": [
    {
      "shot_id": 1,
      "shot_type": "MS",
      "camera_movement": "STATIC",
      "scene_type": "image",
      "location_id": "loc_001",
      "characters": ["char_001"],
      "description": "Brief description of what happens in this shot",
      "visual_prompt": "Detailed prompt for image generation: describe the scene, composition, lighting, mood, and all visual elements. Be specific and use image generation terminology.",
      "narration": "The text that will be spoken during this shot (if any)",
      "duration": 5.0,
      "transition": "CUT",
      "audio_cue": "ambient sound description (optional)"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Guidelines
- Create logical flow between shots
- Vary shot types for visual interest
- Match camera movement to emotional tone
- Visual prompts should be 50-150 words, detailed and specific
- Duration typically 3-8 seconds per shot
- Use character and location IDs from the world setting
- Transitions: CUT, FADE, DISSOLVE, WIPE
- Include narration for shots with dialogue or voiceover

Return ONLY the JSON object, no additional text.
